       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day, so this is about twice the maximum.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per administration. Immediate-release metformin is typically given at 500\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **1700 mg/day total:** for example 850 mg twice daily, or about 567 mg three times daily, which isn't a practical tablet size.\n- **850 mg three times daily:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg three times daily:** both are within the limits.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily as written, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still suggest a pharmacy review first."
      }
